A5  The tetrahedron's own moves.  A peel step by ratio z on one face book: multiply that book by z, keep the point in the solid.
    Kill (a): the step changes any own distance by more than 1e-11 (then it is not the solid's own motion)
    Kill (b): step length is not 1/2 ln z, or two steps on one book do not add, to 1e-11
    Kill (c): the loop A B A^-1 B^-1 on two different books fails to close by more than 1e-11 at any z (then the tetrahedron HAS a wall)
   (a) worst change of a distance under a step 2.3e-13   pass
   (b) worst step-length / adding error        9.7e-12   pass
   (c) worst loop gap, z = 2, 3, 5, wall, 7, 50  5.3e-13   pass  -> the loop always closes: no wall in the tetrahedron
       same loop in the ball: gap 1.1863 at z = 3, 3.4487 at z = 5, 4.1894 at the wall, 5.0591 at z = 7
